#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use IBM Quantum Compute Service for classical feedforward and control flow, otherwise referred to as dynamic circuits"
msgstr "Gunakan IBM Quantum Compute Service untuk suapan balik klasikal dan aliran kawalan, yang juga dikenali sebagai litar dinamik"

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Execute dynamic circuits"
msgstr "Laksanakan litar dinamik"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<OpenInLabBanner notebookPath=\"guides/execute-dynamic-circuits.ipynb\" />\n"
msgstr "<OpenInLabBanner notebookPath=\"guides/execute-dynamic-circuits.ipynb\" />\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Dynamic circuits are powerful tools with which you can measure qubits in the middle of a quantum circuit execution and then perform classical logic operations within the circuit, based on the outcome of those mid-circuit measurements.  This process is also known as _classical feedforward_. While these are early days of understanding how best to take advantage of dynamic circuits, the quantum research community has already identified a number of use cases, such as the following:\n"
msgstr "Litar dinamik adalah alatan berkuasa yang membolehkan anda mengukur qubit di tengah-tengah pelaksanaan litar kuantum dan kemudian melakukan operasi logik klasikal dalam litar, berdasarkan hasil ukuran pertengahan litar tersebut. Proses ini juga dikenali sebagai _suapan balik klasikal_. Walaupun ini adalah hari-hari awal untuk memahami cara terbaik memanfaatkan litar dinamik, komuniti penyelidikan kuantum telah pun mengenal pasti beberapa kes penggunaan, seperti berikut:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Efficient quantum state preparation, such as [GHZ state](https://journals.aps.org/prxquantum/abstract/10.1103/PRXQuantum.5.030339), [W-state](https://arxiv.org/abs/2403.07604) (for more information about W-state, also refer to [\"State preparation by shallow circuits using feed forward\"](https://arxiv.org/abs/2307.14840)), and a broad class of [matrix product states](https://arxiv.org/abs/2404.16083)\n"
msgstr "Penyediaan keadaan kuantum yang cekap, seperti [keadaan GHZ](https://journals.aps.org/prxquantum/abstract/10.1103/PRXQuantum.5.030339), [keadaan W](https://arxiv.org/abs/2403.07604) (untuk maklumat lanjut tentang keadaan W, juga rujuk [\"State preparation by shallow circuits using feed forward\"](https://arxiv.org/abs/2307.14840)), dan kelas luas [keadaan produk matriks](https://arxiv.org/abs/2404.16083)\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "[Efficient long-range entanglement](https://journals.aps.org/prxquantum/abstract/10.1103/PRXQuantum.5.030339) between qubits on the same chip by using shallow circuits\n"
msgstr "[Pembelengguan jarak jauh yang cekap](https://journals.aps.org/prxquantum/abstract/10.1103/PRXQuantum.5.030339) antara qubit pada cip yang sama menggunakan litar cetek\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Efficient [sampling of IQP-like circuits](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2505.04705)\n"
msgstr "[Pensampelan litar seperti IQP yang cekap](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2505.04705)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "These improvements brought by dynamic circuits, however, come with trade-offs. Mid-circuit measurements and classical operations typically have longer execution time than two-qubit gates, and this increase in time might negate the benefits of reduced circuit depth. Therefore, reducing the length of mid-circuit measurement is a focus area of improvement as IBM Quantum&reg; releases the [new version](/guides/changelog-quantum-compute-service#new-version-dynamic-circuits) of dynamic circuits.  For other restrictions when using dynamic circuits, see the [Estimator](/guides/estimator-options#options-compatibility-table) or [Sampler](/guides/sampler-options#options-compatibility-table) Feature compatibility table.\n"
msgstr "Walau bagaimanapun, penambahbaikan yang dibawa oleh litar dinamik ini datang dengan pertukaran. Ukuran pertengahan litar dan operasi klasikal biasanya mempunyai masa pelaksanaan yang lebih lama berbanding Gate dua-Qubit, dan peningkatan masa ini mungkin mengatasi manfaat kedalaman litar yang dikurangkan. Oleh itu, mengurangkan panjang ukuran pertengahan litar adalah bidang tumpuan penambahbaikan apabila IBM Quantum&reg; mengeluarkan [versi baru](/guides/changelog-quantum-compute-service#new-version-dynamic-circuits) litar dinamik. Untuk sekatan lain apabila menggunakan litar dinamik, lihat jadual Keserasian Ciri [Estimator](/guides/estimator-options#options-compatibility-table) atau [Sampler](/guides/sampler-options#options-compatibility-table).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The [OpenQASM 3 specification](https://openqasm.com/language/classical.html#looping-and-branching) defines a number of control-flow structures, but IBM Quantum Compute Service currently only supports the conditional `if` statement. In Qiskit SDK, this corresponds to the [if_test](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit#if_test) method on [QuantumCircuit](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit). This method returns a [context manager](https://docs.python.org/3/reference/datamodel.html#with-statement-context-managers) and is typically used in a `with` statement. This guide describes how to use this conditional statement.\n"
msgstr "[Spesifikasi OpenQASM 3](https://openqasm.com/language/classical.html#looping-and-branching) mentakrifkan beberapa struktur aliran kawalan, tetapi IBM Quantum Compute Service kini hanya menyokong pernyataan `if` bersyarat. Dalam Qiskit SDK, ini sepadan dengan kaedah [if_test](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit#if_test) pada [QuantumCircuit](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit). Kaedah ini mengembalikan [pengurus konteks](https://docs.python.org/3/reference/datamodel.html#with-statement-context-managers) dan biasanya digunakan dalam pernyataan `with`. Panduan ini menerangkan cara menggunakan pernyataan bersyarat ini.\n"

